0	section	Talking to Dr Fenkenstrain
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Have you come to apply for the job?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Yes, if it pays well.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I'll have to ask you some questions first.
2	line	Player	Okay...
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	How would you describe yourself in one word?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Stunning
3	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Mmmm, I see.
3	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I'm sorry, but I don't think you have the aptitude for this position.
3	action	end
2	option	Awe-inspiring
3	action	above
2	option	Breathtaking
3	action	above
2	option	Braindead
3	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Mmmm, I see.
3	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Just one more question. What would you say is your greatest skill?
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Combat
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Mmmm, I see.
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I'm sorry, but I don't think you have the aptitude for this position.
4	action	end
3	option	Magic
4	action	above
3	option	Cooking
4	action	above
3	option	Grave-digging
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Mmmm, I see.
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Looks like you're just the [man/woman] for the job! Welcome aboard!
4	line	Player	Is there anything you'd like me to do for you, sir?
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Yes, there is. You're highly skilled at grave-digging, yes?
4	line	Player	Err...yes, that's what I said.
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Excellent. Now listen carefully.
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I need you to find some...stuff...for me.
4	line	Player	Stuff?
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	That's what I said...stuff.
4	line	Player	What kind of stuff?
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Well...dead stuff.
4	line	Player	Go on...
4	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I need you to get me enough dead body parts for me to stitch together a complete body, which I plan to bring to life.
4	line	Player	Right...okay...if you insist.
4	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	No thanks, I wouldn't work here if you paid me.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Charming.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Dr Fenkenstrain again
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Do you know where I could find body parts?
2	line	Player	Do you know where I could find body parts?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	The soil of Morytania is unique in its ability to preserve the bodies of the dead, which is one reason why I have chosen to carry out my experiments here.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I recommend digging up some graves in the local area. To the south-east you will find the Haunted Woods; I believe there are many graves there.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	There is also a mausoleum on an island west of this castle. I expect the bodies that are buried there to be extremely well preserved, as they were wealthy in life.
2	action	end
1	option	Remind me what you want me to do.
2	line	Player	What do you want me to do, again?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I need you to get me enough dead body parts for me to stitch together a complete body, which I plan to bring to life.
2	line	Player	Right...okay...if you insist.
2	action	end
1	option	Why are you trying to make this creature?
2	line	Player	Why do you want to make a creature?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I came to the land of Morytania many years ago, to find a safe sanctuary for my experiments. This abandoned castle suited my purposes exactly.
2	line	Player	What were you experimenting in?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Oh, perfectly innocent experiments - for the good of mankind.
2	line	Player	Then why did you need to come to Morytania?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Enough questions, now. Get back to your work.
2	action	end
1	option	Will this creature put me out of a job?
2	line	Player	Will this creature put me out of a job?
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	No, my friend. I have a very special purpose in mind for this creature.
2	action	end
1	option	I must get back to work, sir.
2	line	Player	I must get back to work, sir.
2	action	end
0	section	Decapitated head
0	section	Talking to the Gardener Ghost before getting the job
1	cond	If the player is not wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
2	line	Player	Who are you?
2	box	The Headless Gardener's neck twitches at you, but the lack of any head prevents him from speaking.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Gardener Ghost
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Tell me about Fenkenstrain.
2	line	Player	Can you tell me anything about Fenkenstrain?
2	cond	If the player is not wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	box	The Headless Gardener's neck twitches at you, but the lack of any head prevents him from speaking.
2	cond	If the player is wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	box	You feel power emanate from the Amulet of Ghostspeak, and the air around you vibrates with the ghostly voice of the Headless Gardener...
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Oi could tell you a few things about old Fenky, yeah.
3	line	Player	Go on.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Once, this castle were full o' good folk - my friends. Fenky was just the castle doctor you know, to the Lord and the castle folk.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	I don't know what happened to them all, but one by one they all disappeared. When they were gone a while, I went an dug graves for 'em, in the forest.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	After a while there weren't no-one left, but the Lord, Fenkenstrain, and meself.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Old Fenky sent me into the Forest to dig 'im a pit. Never said what for. Then would you believe it, someone chops me head off.
3	line	Player	Did you see who did it, before ...
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Before oi kicked the bucket, you mean?
3	line	Player	Umm...
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Don't worry yourself, I'm not worried about bein' dead. Worse things could happen, I suppose.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	One thing I do know is, there ain't no Lord of the castle anymore, 'cept for old Fenky. Makes you think a bit, don't it?
3	action	end
1	option	What happened to your head?
2	line	Player	What happened to your head?
2	cond	If the player is not wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	action	above
2	cond	If the player is wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	box	You feel power emanate from the Amulet of Ghostspeak, and the air around you vibrates with the ghostly voice of the Headless Gardener...
4	line	Gardener Ghost	Oi was in the old 'aunted Forest to the south, diggin' a pit for moi old maaster, old Fenkenstrain, when would you believe it, someone chops me head off. Awful bad luck, weren't it?
4	line	Player	Oh yes, dreadful bad luck.
4	line	Gardener Ghost	So oi thinks to meself, I don't needs any 'ead to be gettin on with me gardenin', long as I got me hands and me spade.
4	line	Player	Would you show me where the place was?
4	cond	If the player already found the head:
5	line	Gardener Ghost	No mate, you've found my head already, oi think.
5	action	end
4	cond	If the player does not have the head:
5	action	The Gardener Ghost follows the player
5	line	Gardener Ghost	Well, oi s'pose oi've got 10 minutes to spare.
5	action	end
1	option	What's your name?
2	line	Player	Can you tell me anything about Fenkenstrain?
2	cond	If the player is not wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	action	above
2	cond	If the player is wearing the amulet of ghostspeak:
3	box	You feel power emanate from the Amulet of Ghostspeak, and the air around you vibrates with the ghostly voice of the Headless Gardener...
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Me name? It's been a moivellous long while, mate, since I had any use for such a thing as a name.
3	line	Player	Don't worry, I was just trying to make conversation.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	No, no, I can't be havin' that - I'll remember in a minute-
3	line	Player	Please, don't worry.
3	line	Gardener Ghost	Lestwit, that's it! Ed Lestwit!
3	action	end
