0	section	Talking to Dr Fenkenstrain after using the conductor
1	line	Player	So did it work, then?
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Yes, I'm afraid it did, {player} - all too well.
1	line	Player	I can't see it anywhere.
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I tricked it into going up to the Tower, and there it remains, imprisoned.
1	line	Player	So the creature wasn't all you'd hoped, then?
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	...oh, what have I done...
1	line	Player	Oh, I see, we're developing a sense of right and wrong now are we?
1	line	Player	Bit late for that, I'd say.
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	I have no control over it! It's coming to get me!
1	line	Player	What do you want me to do about it?
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Destroy it!!! Take the key to the Tower and take back the life I never should have granted!!!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Dr Fenkenstrain again
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	So have you destroyed it?!!?
1	cond	If the player has the Tower key:
2	line	Player	Not yet.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Please, hurry - save me!!!!
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player has lost the Tower key:
2	line	Player	I seem to have lost the Tower key.
2	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Oh, for goodness sake. Here's a copy I had made.
2	action	
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Gardener Ghost after using the conductor
1	line	Player	How are you?
1	line	Gardener Ghost	Same as ever, mate, just getting' on with it regardless.
1	line	Player	Good for you...err...mate.
0	section	Talking to the Creature of Fenkenstrain
1	line	Player	I am commanded to destroy you, creature!
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Oh that's *hic* not very *hic* nice ...
1	line	Player	Are you feeling okay?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Abso *hic* lutely. Never *buuurrp* better.
1	line	Player	You don't look very dangerous.
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	How *hic* do I look?
1	line	Player	You really don't know, do you? Have a look for yourself.
1	box	The creature stumbles over towards the mirror, focuses upon his reflection and...
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	AAAAARRGGGGHHHH!
1	box	The creature becomes instantly sober, horror all too evident in his undead eyes.
1	line	Player	I'm sorry. I suppose I'm partly to blame for this.
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	No - it was him I wager - Fenkenstrain - wasn't it? He's brought me back to life!
1	line	Player	Who are - were - you?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	I was Rologarth, Lord of the North Coast - this castle was once mine. Fenkenstrain was the castle doctor.
1	line	Player	So the castle wasn't really abandoned when he found it?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Is that what he told you? No, no, this castle was once full of people and life. Fenkenstrain advised me to sell them to the vampyres, which - I am sad to say - I did.
1	line	Player	I found your brain in a jar in Canifis, so he must have sold you too.
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Of that I will not speak. There lie memories that should rest with the dead, the living unable to bear them.
1	line	Player	That's it - I'm leaving this dreadful place, whether I get paid or not. Is there anything I can do for you before I leave?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Only one - please stop Fenkenstrain from carrying on his experiments, once and for all, so that no other poor soul has to endure suffering such as that of my people and I.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Creature of Fenkenstrain again
1	line	Player	Do you know how I can stop Fenkenstrain's experiments?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	Take the Ring of Charos from him.
1	line	Player	What is this ring?
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	It was my birthright, passed down to me through the ages, its origin forgotten.
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	The Ring of Charos has many powers, but Fenkenstrain has bent them to his own evil purposes. Without the power of the ring, he will not be able to raise the dead from their sleep.
1	line	Fenkenstrain's Monster	It has one other, extremely important use - it confuses the werewolves' senses, making them believe that they smell one of their own kind. Without the ring, Fenkenstrain will be at their mercy.
1	action	end
0	section	Convincing Dr Fenkenstrain to stop his experiments
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	So have you destroyed it?!!?
1	line	Player	Never, now that he has told me the truth!
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Oh my, oh my, this is exactly what I feared!
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	Why did you have to pick Rologarth's brain of all brains?!?
1	line	Player	I'm through working for you.
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	No!! I refuse to release you!! You must help me build another creature to destroy this dreadful mistake!!
1	action	end
0	section	Stealing the Ring of Charos
1	cond	If the player pickpockets Dr Fenkenstrain:
2	box	You steal the Ring of Charos from Fenkenstrain.
2	action	
2	box	Congratulations, you've completed a quest: Creature of Fenkenstrain
2	action	end
0	section	Post-quest dialogue
0	section	Lord Rologarth
1	line	Rologarth	How goes it, friend?
1	line	Player	I stole the Ring of Charos from Fenkenstrain.
1	line	Rologarth	I saw him climb up into the Tower to hide it. It doesn't matter - soon the werewolves will come for him, and his experiments will be forever ceased.
1	line	Player	Do you want the ring back? It is yours after all.
1	line	Rologarth	No, you keep it, my friend. Werewolves hunger for the scent of live flesh - I have no need for the ring. I have my castle back, if not my soul.
1	action	end
0	section	Dr Fenkenstrain
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	theyrecomingtogetme theyrecomingtogetme...
1	line	Player	It is all you deserve. Lord Rologarth is master of this castle once more. Let him protect you - if he wants to.
1	line	Dr Fenkenstrain	theyrecomingtogetme theyrecomingtogetme...
1	action	end
